"}],[{"text":"MPP/Public Policy"},{"text":"Environmental policy"}],[{"text":"MSc Disaster Management"},{"text":"Environmental risk/disaster planning"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For highly technical laboratory or pollution-monitoring positions, a relevant MSc or technical qualification can be significantly more appropriate than remaining with the BA alone."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant destinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Sweden"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"New Zealand"},{"text":"Denmark"},{"text":"France"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant Master's Programmes"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Environmental Management"},{"text":"Environmental Policy"},{"text":"Environmental Science"},{"text":"Sustainability"},{"text":"Climate Change"},{"text":"Environmental Planning"},{"text":"GIS & Geospatial Science"},{"text":"Environmental Governance"},{"text":"Natural Resource Management"},{"text":"Sustainable Development"}]},{"type":"p","text":"International students can target careers in environmental consulting, sustainability, environmental planning, climate policy, ESG, conservation and environmental data analysis, subject to local work-authorization and professional requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong pathway is:"},{"type":"h","text":"BA Geography & Environmental Planning"},{"type":"h","text":"Environmental/GIS Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Environment Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Environment Officer"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Environment Officer"},{"type":"h","text":"Environmental Compliance Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Environmental Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Head – Environment / Sustainability"},{"type":"h","text":"ESG / Sustainability Director"},{"type":"p","text":"An alternative technical pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","MSc Environme